From 9d6151d350c9e64efe5853935d59ac9bce8f9634 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(app): tool-number follow-ups of #2488

- Split crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs (401 lines): ImportMode
  and ImportReport move to commands/tool_import_report.rs (97 lines),
  re-exported from tool_import, so no path changes. tool_import.rs is
  now 312 lines.
- Split crates/app/tests/tool_numbers.rs (476 lines): the numbers that
  never shift (#2442) and the legacy loads move to
  tests/tool_numbers/stable.rs. The #[test] count goes from 10 to 13.
- Two legacy-load tests: a file whose entity order is not the name order
  (the freeze numbers by name), and a file that mixes a carried number
  with unnumbered tools.
- tool_numbers::numbers no longer gives an unnumbered tool u32::MAX when
  no number is free: the new tool_numbers::assign refuses it by name, and
  numbers() returns a Result. The post and the import propagate the
  refusal, clash() reports it, number_of / next_free read it as None.
- SetToolNumber keeps its number as a u32 (new already refuses None) and
  exposes number(), so the UI status has no dead "number cleared" arm.

Pinned by tool_numbers: an_unnumbered_tool_with_no_free_number_is_refused_by_name,
stable::a_legacy_project_numbers_by_name_order_not_by_document_order,
stable::a_legacy_project_mixing_numbered_and_unnumbered_tools_keeps_both.

Fixes #2517

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
